WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.480
IDOLiSH7.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.150
What a wonderful name.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.380
Thank you.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.880
I thought we could start by 
releasing a debut CD under this—

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.470
You won't be debuting for a while.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.400
What?

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.560
But, shouldn't we debut soon so people can—

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.460
They'll debut after gaining popularity 
through performing concerts.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.750
Consider what you can 
do now to achieve that.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.770
It's up to their manager 
to show what she can do.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.000
I'll do my best.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.140
Hey, Kinako.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.210
<i>It's time for TRIGGER to take the stage.</i>

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:51.000
<i>With overwhelming performances 
and high-level visuals,</i>

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.550
<i>TRIGGER has captivated women across 
the nation in the blink of an eye.</i>

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.760
You must be busy every day.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.340
Kujo-kun, what's your secret 
for dealing with it?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.560
The smiles of our fans.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.080
Yaotome-san?

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.330
Soba?

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:08.670
Soba?

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.340
The most desirable man in Japan 
gets his energy from soba?

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.230
Tsunashi-kun?

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.310
Looking at the ocean.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.090
Listening to the sound of the waves 
makes my mind and body relax.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:24.280
So you say, but isn't there a beautiful 
woman in a swimsuit beside you?

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.960
Ryu's always swimming.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.210
He keeps getting tanner.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.600
Show them your tan lines.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:33.890
Here?

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:34.950
Sure.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.320
It's time for a commercial.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.990
TRIGGER...

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.560
They've been on TV every day lately.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.590
They just debuted last year, too.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.030
All three are very good 
at singing and dancing.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:53.570
Kujo Tenn-kun in particular has even garnered 
the attention of Broadway directors.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.840
It's no wonder they won the JIMA.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.300
JIMA...

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.800
That's the Japan Idol Music Awards 
held at the end of the year, right?

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.850
Yes. They're awarded to the idols 
who shone the brightest that year.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:12.430
TRIGGER won last year's 
new male idol award.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.800
Amazing.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.500
IDOLiSH7 will need to work hard to catch up.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.530
Don't you want them to debut 
soon so everyone can see them?

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:24.340
Yes. Actually, I...

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.430
Proposal

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.440
First Stage

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.390
We're performing at the 
Daiba Outdoor Concert Hall?

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.160
Yes.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.420
We're performing in such 
a large space already?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.040
Unfortunately, it won't 
be your debut concert.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.950
We should still commemorate 
your first concert, though.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.430
I want you to sing and 
dance in a large space.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:51.470
Oh. Is it a big space?

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.930
It fits about three thousand people.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.700
About ten classrooms?

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.090
More like a hundred.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:02:59.750
A hundred?!

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.120
This doesn't feel real.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.640
Are you sure we'll be okay, Manager?

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.050
You'll be fine!

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:08.400
I'll be promoting the concert.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.900
But, we're just—

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.440
Have some confidence!

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.910
Riku-san's singing.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.820
Yamato-san's expressiveness.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.070
Iori-san's perfection.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.100
Mitsuki-san's energy.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:24.940
Huh?

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.490
Sogo-san's utility.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.610
Nagi-san's grace.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.250
Of course.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.940
Tamaki-san's dancing.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.750
I believe you're all good enough 
to stand on the front lines.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:41.650
When you put it like that...

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.680
I don't feel too bad.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.250
Now let's prepare for your first concert!

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.530
Yeah!

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.080
So...

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.970
What's this?

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:56.890
Let's take one more.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.800
They're photos for the official website.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.070
Is my hair okay?

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.460
There's no point in worrying about that now.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.660
Yeah, but...

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.590
Riku-san, is there anything you like?

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:10.340
Huh?

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.500
I thought I'd include profiles.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.670
Uh, I like omelet rice.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.330
And heroes!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.230
Just kidding.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.570
Wow, Nanase-san, you're so wonderful.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:21.780
You're so cool.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.930
God, he pisses me off!

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.440
What do I like?

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.160
That's a difficult question.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.300
Don't be that way.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.860
Well, if I had to choose...

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:33.660
Yes?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.750
Taking it easy, I guess.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:36.790
I see.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.090
Mitsuki-san, what do you like?

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.380
Isn't it obvious?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.820
The legendary idol Zero.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:49.280
Zero? The super idol who suddenly 
disappeared at the peak of his popularity?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.120
Yeah. I even got his autograph 
when I was little.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.160
That's amazing.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.970
I like Zero.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:58.570
Becoming like Zero is my dream.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.180
What do I like?

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.750
Orderliness and tidiness, I guess.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:08.870
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:08.870
<b>Okonomiyaki</b>

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.180
You like cleaning?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.700
Is that weird?

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.880
No, I think that's wonderful.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.800
Thank you.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.830
Nagi-san, what do you like?

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.130
No girl, no life.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.780
I like beautiful women.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:23.020
And all women are beautiful.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.270
Uh, anything else?

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:26.980
<i>MagiCona</i>!

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:29.400
<i>MagiCona</i>? You mean the anime?

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:33.030
<b>Magical Girl 
Magical Cocona</b>

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:33.030
Yes! <i>Magical Girl Magical Cocona</i>.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.470
I'm obsessed with Japanese anime.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:40.630
Building a palace in Akihabara is my dream.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.590
I see.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.530
What do I like?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.270
Yes.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.590
In that case... cool and sharp stationery.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.320
What do you mean, "in that case?"

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.510
You're nitpicky, aren't you?

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.180
Once you start getting popular, 
your fans will send you gifts.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.850
You should probably tell the truth.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.090
Manager.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:06.030
Put together a schedule, make me a superstar, 
and drown me in a sea of stationery.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:09.210
I look forward to enjoying supreme bliss.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.410
Okay...

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.930
What do I like? King Pudding.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.810
That was quick.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.270
King Pudding's the best.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.040
I just bought some at the convenience store!

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:24.250
Oh, right. Could you give 
me your number later?

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.770
Yours is the only one I don't have yet.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:27.920
I don't have one.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.590
What? I'll see if the agency 
can provide you one, then.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.100
Yes!

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.120
My pudding!

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:43.710
It's decent.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.990
I'll kill you!

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.860
Don't move!

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:50.590
Excuse me. Look over here, please.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.470
Oh, Mitsuki. Don't be shy.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.730
You don't need to hide down there.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.150
I'm not hiding!

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.560
This is how tall I am!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.180
Manager, I wanna be in the middle.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.700
Asserting yourself already?

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.870
Are you actually a showoff?

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.050
I'm trying to balance the image.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:10.250
Stay where you are, please.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:13.180
Tch. If only Mikki were bigger...

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:18.550
I've been praying for that since I was five!

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.890
Nii-san, calm down.

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:22.110
Yeah, shut up.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.150
Why is everyone picking on me?!

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.460
Tamaki-kun, apologize.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:28.370
Sorry.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:29.060
You jerk!

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:30.660
Here we go.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.060
Say cheese!

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.080
Okay, I can do this!

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:57.500
Okay. The IDOLiSH7 official 
website is complete!

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.330
Good morning, Manager.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:02.320
Ogami-san, good morning.

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:04.840
We got your fliers fresh off the press.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.420
Here's a sample.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:10.280
<b>First concert scheduled!</b>

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.750
You finished the official website?

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.910
Were you up all night?

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:20.180
I wanted to finish.

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:23.360
I'm glad you're working hard, 
but don't push yourself too—

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.620
Ah, I'm going to hand
 out fliers at the station!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:27.580
Manager!

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.240
Shouldn't you at least wash your face?

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:33.990
<b>As a woman...</b>

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.990
Is it that bad?

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.990
I will.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:33.990
It's bad.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:37.160
I hope I make it in time 
for the morning rush.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.720
Let's pick singing parts.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.760
How should we decide?

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:45.140
Let's just sing a few lines at a time.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.450
Okay, let's begin.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:48.950
Riku, you start.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:52.320
Who, me? G-Got it.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.440
Here I go.

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.930
"It's the beginning Don't look back

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:02.630
There's no time to look around

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:05.660
We found this Chance

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.030
We can't..." Huh?

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.660
Was that your voice?

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.460
Was there something wrong with it?

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.550
No, the opposite.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:17.730
I can't think of anything original 
to say, but you're a great singer.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:20.770
It was moving.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:22.470
R-Really?

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:25.230
Why don't we have Riku sing the hook?

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:25.800
What?

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.830
Riku, sing the other parts as well.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.400
You're our role model.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.200
You can't beat me at dancing.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.880
What are you competing for?

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.360
Let's start again from the top.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:37.530
Okay!

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:41.270
Once we've picked singing 
parts, let's work on dancing.

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:43.290
Yes, once we've picked.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.860
Okay.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.920
Please take one!

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.330
I'm promoting a concert.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.030
Please take one!

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.990
Please take one!

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.700
Please take one...

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:02.130
Thank you so much!

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:04.980
I'm promoting a concert.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.470
Please take one!

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:07.520
Manager!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.000
My girl.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.000
Guys.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.060
That must be hard on your own.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:14.190
We'll help.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.690
How did you find me—

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.500
These are cool fliers.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:19.780
It's like it's not even me.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:22.780
Amazing! These are wonderful.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.580
Being a manager is hard.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.730
You even have to distribute fliers?

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.140
Yeah.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.290
Come on. Hand them out.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.230
Take one, please.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.830
We're promoting a concert!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:37.070
Please take one.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.460
We're holding a concert!

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.160
Thank you.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.740
Hope to see you there.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.610
Manager, you were up all night 
last night, weren't you?

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:47.500
Huh?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:52.510
You were asleep at your desk 
when we arrived this morning.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.590
Iori said...

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:00.690
"I'm worried about letting someone 
like that hand out fliers alone."

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.940
I'm Izumi Iori.

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:01.930
Can you believe that?

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:01.930
Nii-san!

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.040
I didn't say I was worried.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.480
But, if something happened to her...

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.780
Isn't that what you call worried?

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:11.520
You never shut up, do you?

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.860
Let's finish handing these out.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:13.960
Okay!

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.790
A concert, huh?

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.180
Hey, this guy's handsome.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.240
I like this one.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.800
Check it out.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:24.930
It's the real thing!

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.670
G-Good luck!

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:29.480
That was a surprise.

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:30.500
He was so cool.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.090
I know. We're so lucky.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.630
They called me cool.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.490
Riku-kun, you are cool.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:38.490
You should be more confident in yourself.

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:39.930
That's right.

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.510
You're second coolest after me.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.460
No, after me.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.620
After me.

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:51.670
Since I grew up around someone so amazing, 
I'm not used to this kind of thing.

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:53.040
Someone amazing?

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.820
My brother.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.290
He's kind and good at everything.

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:01.500
Before you know it, he's made 
everyone around him happy.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.340
Sounds like a good brother.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:08.380
Sogo-san, you're a lot like my brother.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:09.390
Really?

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:13.130
I hope your brother comes to the concert.

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:15.050
Yeah.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.990
Let's finish handing out these fliers 
while there are still people around.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.230
We're holding a concert!

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.350
Come check it out!

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.280
Take one.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:27.920
Thank you.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.500
Welcome to the IDOLiSH7 official website

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:37.550
Our hits are steadily rising.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.870
I'm so excited for the concert!

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:45.670
Daddy—

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:47.870
I mean, sir.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.750
You're in a good mood.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.260
Is the concert coming along well?

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:54.550
Yes. More people are visiting the website,

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:58.760
and thanks to the boys,
we handed out all those fliers.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.950
Their singing and dancing is 
becoming more synchronized, too.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.820
All that's left is to wait for the concert.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:05.820
How about tickets?

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:11.000
We couldn't set up reservations, so 
we'll only be selling them the day of.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:14.240
But with this big a response, 
I'm sure we'll be fine.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.230
I see.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.840
Nothing. Do your best.

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:21.660
I will!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.490
What?!

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.640
You're sure there isn't some mistake?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:41.420
As it stands, you can count the 
number of guests on two hands.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:44.530
I doubt we'll see any more.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.670
But, that's...

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:51.430
The website and fliers did so well, though...

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.180
That's how it works.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.250
Sir.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:14:01.510
Most people will access a website from 
home or accept a flier they come across.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:08.050
But, actually coming to a concert 
takes a lot more effort.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.530
They're really talented, though!

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.000
They're overwhelming with charm, really!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:14.840
That's right.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.510
Conveying that to everyone else is our job.

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:23.960
And to tell lots of people, 
we need louder voices.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:31.850
You did your best, but a website 
and fliers were too quiet a voice.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.930
Do you understand?

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:36.780
Yes.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:47.260
This was all my fault.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:50.620
Don't worry.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:53.740
I'll stick to pickled plum 
lunches for a while.

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:58.600
Sir, if you don't mind pickles, 
I can make you some at home.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.450
Thanks.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.100
Don't let it get you down, Manager.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:06.050
I've changed my mind about you.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.010
Huh?

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:12.030
You didn't blame the boys 
for the lack of guests.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:19.030
Believing in them until the very end 
is the most important part of our job.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.380
Go see them.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:26.110
Any star would be shocked 
to see empty stands.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:33.900
Talk to them so they don't lose 
their confidence and their shine.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.050
I will.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:38.940
We'll be starting in 15 minutes.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:42.770
I'll sit in the stands and wave 
enough lights for three people.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:44.730
I'll be waving lights for ten.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:47.060
Wow, you're spirited today.

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:49.740
Manager.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:53.040
We're looking forward 
to their first concert.

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:58.780
Thank you.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:02.290
<b>Greenroom</b>

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:02.280
There aren't many guests?

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.290
You mean it's empty?

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.580
I'm sorry.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:12.060
There isn't a single thing wrong with you.

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:14.790
This is all because I was naive.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.040
I'm really sorry!

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:20.750
Huh?

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:24.120
Um...

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.220
We thought this might happen.

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:28.780
Three thousand's too many off the bat.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:31.730
How many came? One? Two?

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.700
Huh? Uh, nine...

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.890
That's about what we expected.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:37.650
Yeah.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:42.990
Okay. Let's throw a dance party 
with our nine guests tonight.

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:46.480
I was nervous, but I've calmed down now.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.500
We just have to do what we always do.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:50.720
Um...

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:51.930
Manager.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:56.680
Thanks for working so hard to 
prepare for our first concert.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:00.240
You haven't had the chance 
to relax recently, have you?

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.430
Have fun tonight.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:03.750
Yes.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:11.800
Let's get this party started so 
our nine guests will come back!

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.720
Great, Mitsuki.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.260
Those are golden words.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.200
After all, they're our fans.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:23.200
We'll just fill the stands 
next time we perform here.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.260
Hands out, guys.

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:26.450
Come on, Manager.

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:27.930
Huh? Me, too?

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:28.870
What are we doing?

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:31.470
Pumping ourselves up.

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:33.260
Yamato-san, give the word.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.790
Why me?

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:36.670
You're the oldest.

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.720
You're our leader.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:41.120
I'm still only 22.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:45.750
I'm not fit to be a leader.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.300
This is our beginning.

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:54.990
For better or for worse, our beginning 
exists only in this moment today.

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:58.310
Let's give everything we've got right now.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:00.490
Let's go!

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:01.840
Yeah!

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:04.960
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:06.600
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:10.110
Racing through time

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.940
Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:19.290
This vivid GENERATiON with you

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:23.130
(One, Two, Three, Four,
Five, Six, Seven, Jump!!!)

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:28.160
It's the beginning Don't look back

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:31.710
There's no time to look away

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:34.800
We found this Chance

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:38.950
We can't let it go

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:42.420
Once we start running it's Non stop!

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:45.930
Changing at dizzying speeds is our Vision

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:52.110
What kind of sight will we be able to grasp

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.870
With you (Hey!)

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:55.710
It plays (Bang!)

00:18:55.710 --> 00:19:00.500
Someday this Melody will (Fly! High! Fly!)

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:03.240
Like it's traveling across the world

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:07.040
Ring out Fly away

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.790
(Alright! Here we go!)

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.670
Making the dream! (Yeah!)

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.380
Making the sky! (Flight!)

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:15.750
Past all others

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:19.260
Step! (Yes!) Step! (Yes!) we'll advance

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:23.050
The future is in our hands

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.720
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.600
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.140
I will deliver

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.940
Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:39.720
This vivid GENERATiON with you

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:47.870
Ryu, you know our fans don't 
like hearing about girls.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:50.600
Sorry. I lost my composure.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.350
You can't even hold a girl's 
hand in your private life.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.210
And then there's you, Tenn.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:02.220
How can you stand to be 
called a modern day angel?

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.740
You're a cold-blooded hedgehog 
with a double personality.

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:12.040
Gaku, you're lucky you became a star by standing 
there with that face and voice of yours.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.570
What? Who's just standing there?

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:17.000
If you were prepared to move forward—

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.260
Guys, stop arguing!

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.710
For me.

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:22.470
For you?

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:23.710
You fancy yourself the heroine?

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:26.710
No, it's not like that.

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:30.320
I want to go home—

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.320
Quiet.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.710
Shoot! (High!) Shoot! (High!)

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:40.050
Pierce through, let's look
for a Brand new WORLD!

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.050
Is that a concert?

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.050
They're good. I wonder who it is.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.970
Diving to dream! (Yeah!)

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:53.390
Our president would probably tell us to stomp
 them before they have a chance to grow.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:49.470
Diving to sky! (Flight!)

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:52.200
Past all others

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.550
Step, step we'll advance

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:58.860
The future is in our hands

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.920
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:02.650
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.110
I will deliver

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:08.030
Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:14.960
This vivid GENERATiON with you

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:19.540
(One, Two, Three, Four,
Five, Six, Seven, Jump!!!)

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:25.100
<i>What awaited them may
 have been just nine people,</i>

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:28.650
<i>but the applause was sky-shattering.</i>

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:40.910
<i>On their first stage, the seven of them 
shone brilliantly like stars—like a rainbow.</i>

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:48.630
<i>Though I was depressed, even I began 
to smile and was waving my hands.</i>

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:55.350
<i>I had received the energy and excitement 
overflowing from the stage</i>

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:57.890
<i>from those seven men who danced so joyously.</i>

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:04.620
Nice to meet you.

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:05.860
We are...

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.180
IDOLiSH7!
